  "assessment": [
    {
      "area": "Actual original route",
      "evidence": "OriginalSourceLoginHost.startBrowser calls the same environment ProductionRulePlatform, retained AnalyzeUrl GET URL/header parsing, live source.browser request and exact presented boolean; no terminal fake UI event, second engine/HTTP transport or credential writer. Nonempty/empty explicit HTML, awaited result/refetch, showBrowser and POST prefetch remain typed unsupported. The original WebViewModel/WebViewActivity plain navigation branch is the supported bounded contract."
    },
    {
      "area": "MainActor and continuation ownership",
      "evidence": "Existing static Presenter owns queue and one OriginalPageTicket. MainActor isolates ticket, controller, queue and continuation state. Receipt is installed before enqueue; accept/resolve clear it before resume. Waiting cancellation removes ticket and ends it; active cancellation marks/cancels work and uses actual controller dismissal/presentation callbacks. End is idempotent and resumes drain waiters once. No semaphore/queue.sync/main blocking added."
    },
    {
      "area": "Real presentation ACK and failure drain",
      "evidence": "startOriginal authorizes before resolving topVC, records MayPresent before UIKit present, records Presented only in UIKit completion, then reauthorizes before ticket.accept. Cancellation/failed second authorization routes closeOriginal. Host catch awaits cancelOriginal(taskID), whose waitUntilEnded waits for actual controller removal/dismiss completion. Normal Host revoke does not call Presenter cancellation; an accepted nonawait page remains in the existing UI owner."
    },
    {
      "area": "Source/task/deadline authority",
      "evidence": "Host validates bounded HTTP(S), header syntax/case duplicates/text budgets; authorizes exact sourceURL bytes against explicit owner/current revision, request cancellation/deadline and the existing binding cancellation token. Rebinding changed source or normal revoke invalidates pending admission. Checks occur before UI and after completion plus before Host ACK; they are snapshots, not an atomic source-store mutation fence."
    },
    {
      "area": "Parent form and plain WK ownership",
      "evidence": "Only new original route uses overFullScreen and sourceRunHandler:nil. This preserves UIKit underlying views by intended platform policy so the original form does not intentionally exit/cancel its producer; SwiftUI actual appearance still awaits SDK. Existing shell installs source Java/window.run only when sourceRunHandler!=nil. Existing clipboard/UI delegate and CookieStore/HTTPCookieStorage remain inherited shell behavior; no old JSC/source parser bridge is installed."
    },
    {
      "area": "Cookie and later page lifetime",
      "evidence": "Initial request includes original analyzed headers and user agent; retained browser performs WebKit/HTTPCookieStorage seeding and CookieStore.shared capture in its existing navigation/Done/Cancel paths. No Cookie committed-effect receipt is fabricated for the already-completed original JVM task. Normal session close/revoke leaves the accepted page and its ordinary UI cookie lifetime intact."
    },
    {
      "area": "Actual Native source regression",
      "evidence": "New eleventh Native LoginInfo method uses LegadoRuntimeProcess.shared/executor/bindPersistentSource and the default real Presenter; no injected success presenter or second Runtime/HostBox. It asserts sourceBrowserPresented, page active after producer+session/revoke, explicit dismissal drains, and credential/header state unchanged. Ten existing identities retained. This method is authored, not executed."
    }
